From edfd553adddd90e531ff68fd43afd2065d56bbba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 04:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] research: pair rules on top of the V_d class support, no-go
 at stage A

The lazy class-side / cell-side Hall pair rules (class_support = 2) were
to be built only if a cheap lane gate left <= 25% of the entries passing
level 2 for the exact test. Counted in the prototype's scalar CLASS_FIX
at level 6 (a2000, a2200, a2400): 66% of them need it ((i) a cell only
one class covers: 50%; (ii) a class with one cell: 47-48%), while only 3%
are dropped. The estimated gated cost is ~23% of the d-first time
(<= 5% wanted), and with the pairs at zero cost the d-first time would be
0.75-0.85 of level 2's (TSC cycles, five sums), against eager level 6 at
1.24-1.58. Stage B not built; the instrumentation is saved as patches in
research/wip/patches/c2-classhall (on be625d8, -DCLASS_SUP only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
