+From 65c6495651794de015bfa7963401738ea87de466 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:10:58 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 2/3] measure: V_d class-matching support (-DCLASS_SUP, env
+ CLASS_SUP/CLASS_LVL/CLASS_VEC; compiled out by default)
+
+Every vector of V_d has exactly one of d's numbers (its class), and the 6
+rows (cols) of a square have the 6 classes. So a candidate's cells outside
+the placed vectors of the other axis need other-axis candidates of
+distinct, unplaced classes (non-d cells: not its own class): a matching.
+Scalar fixpoints (levels 1-6, full Hall = 4) and a vectorized level 2/5/6
+on the class-sorted carried lists (CLASS_VEC), by layer (CLASS_SUP mode).
+Measurement only; default builds unchanged (bench quick 1,770,779 nodes).
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
